    "body": "**Tournament setup** is where you describe the tournament: basics, divisions, venues, fees, registration, pay rates, game timing and the public event page. Settings used to be a separate page; it now opens here.\n\n**Where:** **Setup → Tournament setup**. On a phone, pick the part you want from the **Setup section** dropdown.\n\n**The sections (left side):**\n- Basics: **General info**, **Divisions**, **Venues & fields**\n- Money: **Team fees**, **Registration types**, **Staff pay rates**\n- Play: **Game Timing & Format**, **Standings tiebreakers**\n- Public: **Page builder**, **Tournament info**, **Broadcast permissions**\n\nA check next to a section means it has been filled in. The **Summary** box counts divisions, venues, fields and **Sections done**.\n\n**To edit general info:**\n1. Open **General info**.\n2. Fill in **Tournament Name** (required), **Sport**, **Location**, **Start Date** and **End Date**.\n3. Under **Tournament Logo**, click **Upload Logo** (or **Use from library**). **Remove** clears it.\n4. Click **Save Changes** (top right; at the bottom on a phone).\n\nOne **Save Changes** button saves every section at once, so you can move between sections and save at the end.\n\n**Common problems:**\n- Nothing is saved until you click **Save Changes**.\n- If only part saves, a message names what did NOT save (for example tournament info or the public event page content). Click **Save Changes** again.\n- To place games on fields, use the **Game Scheduler** link under the sections, or **Setup → Scheduler**."
