    "body": "Venues and fields are the places games are played. The Scheduler uses them as its columns, and venues with an address show on the public event page.\n\n**Where:** **Setup → Tournament setup → Venues & fields**.\n\n**To set the default hours:**\n1. Under **Default field availability**, enter a start and end time for each tournament date.\n2. Click **+ Add time slot** to add a second window on the same day.\n\n**To add a venue and its fields:**\n1. Type the venue name in **Venue / complex name** and click **+ Add Venue**.\n2. Add fields: type a number in **How many fields?** to add Field 1, Field 2 and so on, or type one name in **Or add one:** (for example \"2A\" or \"North\").\n3. Rename a field or change its **Abbr** right in the list. The **×** removes a field or venue.\n4. Click **Save Changes**.\n\n**To show a venue to teams and parents:** fill in the street address, and optionally a Google Maps link and a field map image URL. A map appears automatically from the address. Leave the address blank to hide the venue from the public page.\n\n**To give one field its own hours or limits:**\n1. Click **Availability** on that field.\n2. Set **Available Hours** (**From** / **To**) for each day.\n3. Under **Division restrictions**, tick the only divisions allowed on that field. None ticked means **All divisions**.\n\n**Common problems:**\n- To close a field for one day (rain, maintenance), use **Close today** on the Scheduler instead of deleting the field.\n- Nothing is saved until you click **Save Changes**."
